findings.description:
`save_review_file` builds `f"{slice_index}-review.{review_type}.{slice_name}.{ext}"` from an `int` index (`persistence.py:438`). `save_review_result` takes a `SliceInfo` TypedDict (`persistence.py:457`). `resolution_evidence.locate_review(index, ...)` finds reviews by index. The document says a PR-keyed name "satisfies the review frontmatter contract without a slice index" but never says:

- what the name looks like;
- what goes in the frontmatter index field;
- whether `locate_review`, archiving, and digest code (all keyed by index) get a PR-aware lookup.

"Archiving, digest, and integrity checks... apply unchanged" is asserted but not true: every one of them takes an index.

The "configured squadron data directory" is also unnamed: no config key, default, or per-repo layout. Without a default, the first unplanned-repo run fails. With one, the doc should say where it is, as the config rules require. This is the slice the doc says depends on 916/917. It needs the target contract (a protocol with `filename()`, `frontmatter()`, `locate()`) settled here, not deferred.
